{comment: Verse 1}
An [Dm]old cowpoke went ridin' out
One [F]dark and windy day
U[Dm]pon a ridge he rested
As he went along his way.
When all at once a mighty herd
Of red-eyed cows he saw
A-[Bb]plowin' thru the ragged skies,
And [Dm]up a cloudy draw.

{comment: Chorus}
Yip-pi-i-[F]o
Yip-pi-i-[Dm]a,
[Bb]Ghost Riders in the [Dm]Sky.

{comment: Verse 2}
Their [Dm]brands were still on fire,
And their [F]hooves were made of steel
Their [Dm]horns were black and shiny,
And their hot breath he could feel.
A bolt of fear went thru him,
As they thundered thru the sky,
For he [Bb]saw the riders commin' hard,
And he [Dm]heard their mournful cry.

{comment: Skip Chorus}

{comment: Verse 3}
Their [Dm]faces gaunt, their eyes all blurred
Their [F]shirts all soaked with sweat
[Dm]They're ridin' hard to catch that herd
But they ain't caught 'em yet;
For they've got to ride forever,
In that range up in the sky,
On [Bb]horses breathing fire,
As they [Dm]ride on, hear their cry.

{comment: Chorus}

{comment: Verse 4}
As the [Dm]riders loped on past him,
He heard [F]one call his name,
[Dm]"If you want to save your soul from hell
A-ridin' on our range,
Then cowboy, change your way today,
Or with us you will ride,
[Bb]Tryin' to catch the Devil's herd,
A[Dm]cross these endless skies."

{comment: Chorus (repeat)}
